export anchor ModularSynthStyle:
    number: 311
    screen: OpsMonitor
    name: Modular synth
    idea: A rack of synth modules between metal rails, each service a module with an uptime knob, a status lamp and jacks, a patch bay of coloured cables linking the services, and hourly traffic as a step sequencer.
    base: dark
    palette:
        case: #0c0d10, the page behind the rack
        rail: #41454d, rack rails and the style sheet edge
        module: #1b1e25, module faces
        edge: #343a46, module borders and rules
        ink: #eef0f4, silkscreen text and knob pointers
        muted: #a9b0bd, small labels
        sky: #5cc8ff, the api module, p50, Recovered, the primary button and the focus halo
        violet: #c4a3ff, the web module and its cable
        amber: #ffc04d, the sync-worker module, sequencer lights, Degraded and the incident gate
        mint: #6fe0a6, the notifications module, Healthy and Resolved
        pink: #ff8fa8, the billing module and the patch title
        red: #ff7b7b, the error trace and Firing
    type:
        Condensed caps in Roboto Condensed, Arial Narrow, Helvetica Neue,
        Arial, system-ui at 14px, values in ui-monospace, Menlo, Consolas.
        The brand is 22px condensed at 800, uptime values 18px mono bold,
        module titles 13px bold caps tracked 0.14em, labels 10 to 11px caps.
    layout:
        Metal rails with oval holes separate four rack rows. Row one holds
        a narrow brand module with BRIGHTWORK and the apps as a lamp list,
        Ops lit, then one module per service, each with a coloured title
        underline, a knob whose arc shows uptime on a 99 to 100 percent
        scale, the uptime value, a status lamp strip with shape and word,
        the metric and In and Out jacks. Billing shows 6 min down and back
        at 07.54. Row two holds the patch bay, five labelled jacks with
        sagging cables from web to api, api to sync-worker, api to billing
        and sync-worker to notifications, listed below, and the gate module
        for the incident on an amber tinted face. Row three holds the
        sequencer, 24 hourly columns of ten amber lights with the 14.00
        peak lit white, and a scope module with error and latency screens.
        Row four holds triggers for alerts and a clock module for deploys.
        Every module has screws top and bottom. At phone width modules go
        full width and service modules pair up.
    spacing: A 4px gap between modules, 20px module padding top and bottom for screws, 12px sides.
    density: Medium dense. Modules pack edge to edge in rack rows.
    corners: 3px module faces, round knobs, jacks, lamps and screws.
    borders: 1px #343a46 modules, a 3px coloured underline under each title.
    shadows: A soft shadow under cables, glowing lamps and lit steps, a metal gradient on rails.
    icons:
        16px status shapes in lamp strips and lists, a ringed tick for
        Healthy, a triangle for Degraded, a circular arrow for Recovered, a
        bolt for Firing, a tick for Resolved and a magnifier for
        Investigating. Knobs, jacks and screws are drawn decoration.
    focus: A 3px white outline offset 2px with a sky halo.
    tone: Synth module names, such as Patch, Gate, Sequencer, Scope, Triggers and Clock.
